# Design Document Rules

When working in the design directory, follow these rules:

## Format Requirements
- Use Markdown format for design documents
- Follow the template in `docs/design/design-template.md`
- Each design MUST have a unique ID: `DES-XXXX` (4 digits, zero-padded)
- Filename format: `DES-XXXX-descriptive-name.md`

## Mandatory Sections
1. **Overview** - What is being built and why
2. **Goals / Non-goals** - Explicit scope boundaries
3. **Traces to** - MUST list REQ-xxxx and UC-xxxx references
4. **Architecture** - Components, boundaries, interfaces
5. **Test strategy** - How requirements will be verified

## Traceability Requirements
- MUST include `## Traces to` section with explicit REQ-xxxx references
- Every design goal must map to at least one requirement
- No orphan design features (features without requirement backing)

```markdown
## Traces to
- Requirements: REQ-0001, REQ-0002, REQ-0003
- Use cases: UC-0001
```

## Design Quality Checklist
- [ ] All requirements referenced in Traces to section
- [ ] Clear API boundaries and interfaces defined
- [ ] Failure modes documented
- [ ] Concurrency/threading model specified (if applicable)
- [ ] Test strategy covers all referenced requirements
- [ ] At least one alternative considered

## After Creating/Editing Design Docs
1. Run: `python tools/traceability/check_traceability.py --docs docs --tests tests`
2. Request CDR (Critical Design Review) for significant changes

## Related Agents
- Use `agents/design-author.md` for creating design documents
- Use `agents/cdr-reviewer.md` for design review
